# m2asc frontend style

Conventions for `{Ng}` (Angular). Keep bullets short; expand only when a pattern is repeated.

## Services

- Injectable services live under `src/app/services/` (not feature folders like `conversion/`)
- File name matches the service (e.g. `convert-api.service.ts`)

## Models co-located with services

- Small types/DTOs used primarily by one service belong in that service’s file (e.g. `ConvertOptions` with `ConvertApiService`)
- Split a model into its own file only when shared across unrelated features or it grows real behavior

## Domain constants

- Shared domain constants (not service DTOs) live under `src/app/constants/` (e.g. `ascii-charsets.ts`)

## Components

- Prefer single-file components (inline template/styles in the `.ts` file)
- Do not nest a single-file component in its own subfolder — place flat under `src/app/components/` (e.g. `components/upload-zone.ts`, not `components/upload-zone/upload-zone.ts`)
- Use a subfolder only when the component truly has multiple sibling files

## Accessibility markup

- Do not add ARIA / a11y attributes (`aria-*`, `role` for assistive tech, `sr-only` a11y helpers, etc.)
- Prefer plain semantic HTML and visible labels; skip screen-reader-only affordances in this app
